      "writtenOn": "2023-02-14T07:51:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you rely on mBuilderMap to cleanup upstream variables, then this would be wrong if user quickly off/on tethering. Here is the case:\n1. User enable wifi tethering, then stop wifi tethering\n2. At the moment user stop wifi tethering, usb tethering start.\n3. Tethering upstream code path is doing stop process and calling #cleanup() but finding usb type builder is there then skip cleanup.\n4. Tethering upstream code path start again but previous mUpstreamEventList which used for wifi tethering don\u0027t be cleared.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 245,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 245,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "01c591c50d2d24fa4f3594226d85e5f2864db888",
